ts are cut to fit it", "group": "Sheet and laser", "order": 2, "min": "1.5 mm", "max": "6.5 mm", "step": "0.05 mm", "unit": "mm"}], ["variable.publish", {"name": "laser_kerf", "label": "Laser kerf", "description": "How much wood your beam burns away, from a test cut; the slots are drawn narrower by this much", "group": "Sheet and laser", "order": 3, "min": "0 mm", "max": "0.4 mm", "step": "0.01 mm", "unit": "mm"}], ["variable.publish", {"name": "slot_play", "label": "Slot play", "description": "How much wider than the other sheet a slot comes out: 0 a tight press fit, 0.1 mm snug, 0.2 mm slides together easily", "group": "Sheet and laser", "order": 4, "min": "0 mm", "max": "0.4 mm", "step": "0.01 mm", "unit": "mm"}], ["variable.publish", {"name": "lift", "label": "Lift the walnut slices (view only)", "description": "Lifts the walnut slices off to show how the two families slide together; the cut sheets do not change", "group": "View", "order": 1, "min": "0", "max": "100", "step": "1"}], ["document.info", {"title": "Sliceform sculpture", "description": "A sliceform: two families of laser-cut plywood slices, birch one way and walnut the other, that slide into each other with half-lap slots and together show a surface from a formula: a saddle, a ripple or a ball. Choose the shape, its size, the number of slices each way, your two sheets as measured, your laser's kerf and the play of the slots. Every slot meets its partner half way up its crossing. To cut it: File > Export..., SVG or DXF, Sheet of set \"Cut sheet, birch\" and then \"Cut sheet, walnut\", with your laser bed's width as the sheet width; every slice is on a layer of its own (Birch slice 1 ... and Walnut slice 1 ...).", "author": "3DCraft Jigs", "licence": "CC-BY-4.0", "url": "https://github.com/johancoppens/3dcraft-jigs/tree/main/jigs/sliceform", "tags": ["sliceform", "sculpture", "laser cutting", "plywood", "half-lap", "mathematics"]}], ["variable.set", {"name": "birch_slices", "expr": "7"}], ["variable.set", {"name": "walnut_slices", "expr": "7"}], ["variable.set", {"name": "birch_slices", "expr": "12"}], ["variable.set", {"name": "birch_thickness", "expr": "1.5 mm"}], ["variable.set", {"name": "height", "expr": "570 mm"}], ["variable.set", {"name": "shape", "expr": "3"}], ["variable.set", {"name": "walnut_slices", "expr": "12"}], ["variable.set", {"name": "walnut_thickness", "expr": "1.5 mm"}], ["variable.set", {"name": "width", "expr": "600 mm"}], ["variable.set", {"name": "laser_kerf", "expr": "0.4 mm"}], ["variable.set", {"name": "slot_play", "expr": "0.4 mm"}], ["document.check", {}]]